## Calling C Functions from XIOM

The **Foreign Function Interface (FFI)** lets XIOM call C libraries using `extern "C"` declarations.

### Declaring External Functions

```xiom
extern "C" {
  fn abs(x: Int) -> Int;
  fn strlen(s: *const Char) -> Int;
  fn malloc(size: Int) -> *mut Unit;
  fn free(ptr: *mut Unit) -> Unit;
}
```

### Calling C Functions

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let x = -42;
  let result = abs(x);  // calls C's abs()
  return result;
}
```

External function calls are inherently `unsafe` — the compiler can't verify the C code:

```xiom
unsafe {
  let ptr = malloc(100);  // allocate 100 bytes
  // use ptr...
  free(ptr);              // free the memory
}
```

### C Type Mapping

| C Type | XIOM Type |
|--------|-----------|
| int | Int |
| float | Float32 |
| double | Float64 |
| char* | *const Char |
| void* | *mut Unit |
| size_t | Int |

### Linking

C libraries are linked by listing them in the project manifest:

```xiom
// Link to libm (math library)
extern "C" {
  #[link(name = "m")]
  fn sqrt(x: Float64) -> Float64;
  fn pow(base: Float64, exp: Float64) -> Float64;
}
```

### Basic FFI Pattern

```xiom
// 1. Declare the C function
extern "C" {
  fn getpid() -> Int;
}

// 2. Wrap in a safe function
fn current_pid() -> Int {
  unsafe { return getpid(); }
}
```

